FPL AI — PHASE 2A: HISTORICAL DATASET CONSTRUCTION

Phase 1C is officially complete.

The deterministic/statistical baseline is now fixture-aware, has proper team-strength ratings, has passed its current validation suite, and has been confirmed to use only pre-GW1 2026/27 information.

We are now beginning the ML pipeline.

IMPORTANT:

Do NOT train any ML models yet.

Do NOT modify the optimizer.

Do NOT modify the current projection formulas.

Do NOT modify the current team-strength model.

Do NOT add RAG, news, ownership, Monte Carlo, or other features.

This phase has ONE objective:

BUILD A CLEAN, HISTORICAL, PRE-DEADLINE, LEAK-FREE DATASET THAT CAN LATER BE USED TO TRAIN THE EXPECTED-MINUTES MODEL.

==================================================
OBJECTIVE
==================================================

We eventually want to predict:

1. P(start)
2. Expected minutes
3. P(60+ minutes)
4. P(0 minutes)

for every player before an FPL gameweek deadline.

Before training anything, we need historical snapshots representing exactly what would have been known BEFORE each historical gameweek.

The dataset must therefore be constructed chronologically.

Each row should represent:

PLAYER + GAMEWEEK + PRE-DEADLINE INFORMATION

with the actual outcome stored separately as the target.

